// The fused build ran out of memory, the node-walk gave 100 (soak nov25a).
// `x` is a parameter no value reaches, so it takes the type its uses demand:
// the array's element type, which holds the callback, whose `acc` is a map of
// what `x` flows into. Fixed at that, `x` held itself, and the first walk of
// the type never ended. A demand that holds a cell the parameter flows into
// names the parameter itself, and decides nothing.
// Expected trace (both engines): 100.
{ |x| [x, cast<string>(x), `N("foobarbaz"), |acc, (k, v)| map::insert(acc, k, x)]; 100 }
